.\" mailut.conf(5) -- Mailu Tools configuration
.TH MAILUT.CONF 5 "2026-09-17" "Mailu Tools 1.0.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
mailut.conf \- configuration file for Mailu Tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/mailut/mailut.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mailut.conf
configures
.BR mailut (8).
It is an INI file: sections in square brackets, then
.I key = value
lines. A
.B #
or
.B ;
begins a comment, including at the end of a value. Values are not expanded or
interpolated, and the file is never executed or sourced.
.PP
Booleans accept
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off
and
.BR 1 / 0 .
Lists are separated by commas or whitespace. An unknown section or key is a
hard error rather than a silent no-op, so a typo cannot quietly disable a
setting.
.PP
This file holds
.B static host configuration only.
Audit collection scopes are mutable state and live in the SQLite database;
manage them with
.B mailut audit add
and
.BR "mailut audit remove" .
The configuration file is not a database.
.PP
An example with every default is installed at
.IR /usr/local/share/mailut/mailut.conf.example .
.B make install
and
.B mailut upgrade
never overwrite an existing
.IR /etc/mailut/mailut.conf .
Keep the file mode 0640 or stricter.
.PP
Validate it at any time with
.BR "mailut config check" ,
and print every effective value with
.BR "mailut config show" .
.SH SECTION [mailu]
.TP
.B compose_dir
Directory containing the Mailu
.IR docker-compose.yml .
Default:
.IR /opt/mailu .
.TP
.B compose_command
Command used to talk to Compose, split on whitespace and executed as an
argument vector. Use
.I docker-compose
for the legacy v1 binary. Default:
.IR "docker compose" .
.TP
.B smtp_service
Name of the Postfix service in the compose file. Default:
.IR smtp .
.TP
.B front_service
Name of the front proxy service, whose log carries real client IP addresses.
Default:
.IR front .
.TP
.B antispam_service
Name of the Rspamd service. Default:
.IR antispam .
.TP
.B local_domains
Optional list of domains this server accepts mail for. When set, the
.B all
audit scope matches only recipients at these domains, which keeps outbound
recipients out of the audit. When empty, the
.B all
scope matches every inbound recipient observed. Default: empty.
.SH SECTION [storage]
.TP
.B state_dir
Base directory for all state. Empty means the installed layout's state
directory,
.IR /var/lib/mailut .
Default: empty.
.TP
.B database
Path to the SQLite database. Empty means
.IR <state_dir>/mailut.sqlite3 .
Default: empty.
.TP
.B message_dir
Directory holding gzipped raw messages. Empty means
.IR <state_dir>/messages .
Default: empty.
.TP
.B backup_dir
Directory holding database backups taken before a schema migration. Empty means
.IR <state_dir>/backups .
Default: empty.
.TP
.B busy_timeout_ms
SQLite busy timeout in milliseconds, applied to every connection. Default:
.IR 5000 .
.SH SECTION [audit]
.TP
.B default_retention_days
Metadata retention, in days, for records created by a scope that does not
override it. Each record stores its own expiry when it is created, so changing
this affects future records only. Minimum 1. Default:
.IR 30 .
.TP
.B default_level
Collection level used when
.B mailut audit add
is called without
.BR \-\-level :
.BR metadata ,
.B headers
or
.BR message .
It must be permitted by
.B allow_headers
/
.B allow_messages
below. Default:
.IR metadata .
.TP
.B store_accepted
Record accepted and delivered inbound mail as metadata, not only rejections.
Turning this off makes it impossible to tell "this server never saw it" from
"this server accepted it". Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B allow_headers
Permit scopes to collect at level
.BR headers .
When false, a new scope may not ask for it: the request fails rather than being
downgraded. A scope created while it was permitted keeps its recorded level but
collects only metadata, which
.B mailut audit scopes
and
.B mailut doctor
both report. Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B allow_messages
Permit scopes to collect at level
.BR message ,
retaining complete original messages. Off by default because it retains the
contents of other people's mail. Default:
.IR false .
.TP
.B message_retention_days
Retention, in days, for stored raw messages when a scope does not override it
with
.BR \-\-message\-retention .
May be shorter than the metadata retention, in which case the body is deleted
while the metadata remains. Minimum 1. Default:
.IR 30 .
.TP
.B message_max_bytes
Largest message that will be stored. A larger one is not truncated: its
metadata is kept and the omission is recorded in the event's reason. Minimum
1024. Default:
.I 26214400
(25 MiB).
.TP
.B max_retention_days
Upper bound accepted by
.B \-\-retention
and
.BR \-\-message\-retention .
Default:
.I 3650
(10 years).
.SH SECTION [collector]
.TP
.B bind
Address the audit collector listens on. The collector is unauthenticated, so it
must not be reachable from other hosts.
.IP
A loopback address is the safest, but the Rspamd exporter runs inside the
antispam container and cannot reach the host's loopback. For that case bind to
an address the container can reach and the outside world cannot \(em normally
the Docker bridge gateway, such as
.IR 172.17.0.1 .
Whatever you choose must match the
.B url
in the exporter snippet.
.IP
A wildcard
.RB ( 0.0.0.0 ", " :: )
or a publicly routable address is refused unless
.B "mailut audit collect \-\-allow\-remote"
is used deliberately. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B port
TCP port for the collector, 1\-65535. Default:
.IR 8765 .
.TP
.B max_body_bytes
Largest accepted HTTP request body. A larger request is refused with 413.
Minimum 4096. Default:
.I 4194304
(4 MiB).
.TP
.B log_poll_seconds
How often the Mailu smtp container log is polled. One Docker call per poll,
never one per event. Minimum 1. Default:
.IR 30 .
.TP
.B log_lookback
How far back the log is read the first time, before a cursor exists. Accepts a
duration such as
.IR 10m ", " 2h ", " 1d .
Default:
.IR 10m .
.TP
.B ingest_smtp_logs
Whether the collector polls the Postfix log at all. Set to false to collect
Rspamd decisions only \(em at the cost of losing every pre-DATA and policy
rejection, which Rspamd never sees. Default:
.IR true .
.SH SECTION [watch]
.B mailut watch
samples the queue and recent SMTP activity and compares each value against a
warning and a critical threshold. A value strictly above
.I *_warn
raises a warning; strictly above
.I *_crit
a critical.
.TP
.B window
Log window used for rate calculations, as a duration. Default:
.IR 15m .
.TP
.B retention_days
How long recorded samples are kept, in days. Expired samples are deleted by
.BR "mailut audit purge \-\-expired" .
Default:
.IR 90 .
.TP
.BR queue_warn ", " queue_crit
Total messages in the Postfix queue. Defaults:
.IR 200 ", " 500 .
.TP
.BR deferred_warn ", " deferred_crit
Messages in the deferred queue. Defaults:
.IR 100 ", " 300 .
.TP
.BR sender_sent_warn ", " sender_sent_crit
Messages submitted by one authenticated (SASL) sender within
.BR window .
Defaults:
.IR 50 ", " 150 .
.TP
.B bulk_sender_msgs
A sender submitting at least this many messages within
.B window
counts as bulk-like. Default:
.IR 50 .
.TP
.BR multi_sender_warn ", " multi_sender_crit
How many distinct bulk-like senders at once are suspicious. A credential dump
shows up as several accounts sending together with no single one dominating.
Defaults:
.IR 3 ", " 5 .
.TP
.BR sender_queue_warn ", " sender_queue_crit
Messages queued by one envelope sender, point in time. Defaults:
.IR 100 ", " 300 .
.TP
.BR rcpt_domains_warn ", " rcpt_domains_crit
Distinct recipient domains addressed by one sender in the queue. Defaults:
.IR 25 ", " 50 .
.TP
.BR bounce_defer_rate_warn ", " bounce_defer_rate_crit
Bounce plus defer rate over
.BR window ,
as a percentage of delivery attempts. Defaults:
.IR 20 ", " 40 .
.TP
.BR spam_block_warn ", " spam_block_crit
Remote spam or blacklist rejections seen within
.BR window .
Defaults:
.IR 1 ", " 5 .
.PP
The defaults suit a busy server. For a low-volume transactional host they are
far too high; lower them until a sample of normal traffic sits comfortably
below the warning level.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[mailu]
compose_dir = /opt/mailu
compose_command = docker compose
smtp_service = smtp
front_service = front
antispam_service = antispam
local_domains = example.com, example.org

[storage]
state_dir = /var/lib/mailut
database = /var/lib/mailut/mailut.sqlite3

[audit]
default_retention_days = 30
default_level = metadata
store_accepted = true
allow_headers = true
allow_messages = false
message_retention_days = 30
message_max_bytes = 26214400

[collector]
bind = 127.0.0.1
port = 8765
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mailut/mailut.conf
The configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/mailut/mailut.conf.example
The shipped example, with every setting at its default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mailut (8)
